.TH "cbor::item" 3 "Version 0.9.0" "mbedded-cbor" \" -*- nroff -*-
.ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
cbor::item \- One node of a tree from \fBcbor::decode()\fP or \fR\fBlazy::clone\fP\fP\&.  

.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.PP
\fR#include <cbor/item\&.hpp>\fP
.SS "Public Member Functions"

.in +1c
.ti -1c
.RI "template<cbor::type K> std::expected< item_alternative_t< K >, \fBerror\fP > \fBget\fP () const"
.br
.RI "Gives the value of the node when \fRtype\fP is \fRK\fP\&. "
.in -1c
.SS "Public Attributes"

.in +1c
.ti -1c
.RI "cbor::type const \fBtype\fP"
.br
.ti -1c
.RI "std::uint8_t const \fBadditional_information\fP"
.br
.in -1c
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP 
One node of a tree from \fBcbor::decode()\fP or \fR\fBlazy::clone\fP\fP\&. 

\fRtype\fP gives the kind of the node\&. \fRadditional_information\fP gives the low 5 bits of the initial byte (RFC 8949 3)\&. \fBcbor::item::get()\fP gives the value\&. The constructor is private: only a decode makes an item\&. An item owns no memory and has no destructor to run\&. The tree owns every node and every string\&. An item gives no error\&. \fRtype\fP and \fRadditional_information\fP are data members\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
(*tree)\->type                     → cbor::type const
(*tree)\->additional_information   → std::uint8_t const
(*tree)\->get<cbor::type::array>() → std::expected<std::span<item const>, error>
.fi
.PP
 
.PP
.nf
message: [1, {"a": 2}]
call: auto const tree = cbor::decode(bytes)
result: owning item of [1, {"a": 2}]
call: (*tree)\->type
result: cbor::type::array
call: (*tree)\->additional_information
result: 2
call: (*tree)\->get<cbor::type::array>()\->size()
result: 2

.fi
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
    // bytes: a std::string with [1, {"a": 2}]
    auto const tree = cbor::decode(bytes);
    auto const kind = (*tree)\->type;                              // cbor::type::array
    auto const count = (*tree)\->get<cbor::type::array>()\->size();  // 2
.fi
.PP
 
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBcbor::item::get()\fP 

.PP
\fBcbor::decode()\fP 

.PP
\fBcbor::encode()\fP 
.RE
.PP

